# E2E

E2E is a smoke of the main user action, not branch coverage. Branches stay in unit tests (`.test.ts`).

## When

MUST write or update one spec when the task is major AND it changes UI.

Major means any one of:

- a new `page.tsx` under `apps/web/src/app/(`
- a new user action (button, form, or navigation that changes data)
- the PLAN row lists two or more AC and at least one describes a user action

MUST NOT write e2e for:

- backend-only work
- a small UI tweak (copy, style, reorder, a fix on an existing screen with no new action)
- TBD tasks (P-08, P-18)

## How

- One file, one happy path: open, do the main action, see the result. A few steps only. No validation errors, empty states, or permission branches.
- Assert with `getByRole` and a name, plus visible text. No pixels, no `toHaveScreenshot`, no screenshots in git, no `waitForTimeout`, no `data-testid` as the norm.
- No page objects until two specs share code.
- Naming: `e2e/{context}/{verb}-{object}.spec.ts`, singular context folder matching `apps/web/src/client/modules/`.
- If the flow needs saved records, add or reuse a seed helper in `e2e/shared/seed/`. The spec does not import `packages/database` directly when a helper can do it. Do not implement the P-15 widget-to-dashboard scenario as part of another task.
- Playwright `screenshot` and `video` stay off. Output goes to gitignored `test-results/` and `playwright-report/`.

## Running

- `pnpm test:e2e` (config: `e2e/playwright.config.ts`).
- Do not add an e2e job to CI. The loop runs `pnpm test:e2e` on the implementer machine before push only when the diff contains a file under `e2e/`.
